trong>57\u00b0F</strong> was the 6th warmest November 13 high of 108 since 1906, the warmest since 2025. The normal high for the date is 41\u00b0F, and the record is 61\u00b0F (1990, 1999). The low of <strong>26\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If McCall's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, McCall has set <strong>49 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 89 that chance alone would give, and <strong>77 record highs</strong>, close to the 89 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (68). McCall's all-time high is 104\u00b0F, on August 10, 1928.","t_chg":"McCall's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 92 complete years: McCall's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.29\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.16 to +0.41), about +3.4\u00b0F since 1907. McCall's average high shows no clear change: +0.02\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.12 to +0.15) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 9 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months.","t_rain":"McCall has gotten drier","p_rain":"McCall's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.41 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.74 to \u22120.08), about \u22124.8 inches since 1907. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 22.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 1951 (36.13 in); the driest, 2002 (13.05 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}